      "message": "test(ui): measure the machine action row at the page's visible bottom\n\nThe page's buttons must be reachable without a scroll in a 720 px window.\n\nThe old assertion compared each action button's bottom with the bottom of\nthe Properties leaf. That is the wrong edge: pages.rs gives the page's\nScrollArea the leaf height minus 40 px, and draws the separator and the\nClose footer inside that bottom 40 px band. A button can therefore stand\nunder the fold and still pass.\n\nThe test now reads the top of the Close footer from the Properties pane\nand compares each button's bottom against it, with a 1 px tolerance.\n\nReview measurement at 1280x720 (head c555b4eea):\n\n  leaf        [[990.0 104.0] - [1264.0 682.0]]\n  Close       [[996.0 648.0] - [1035.5 666.0]]\n  Load other  [[1016.0 644.0] - [1091.3 668.0]]\n  Edit        [[1099.3 644.0] - [1174.7 668.0]]\n  Clear       [[1182.7 644.0] - [1258.0 668.0]]\n\nThe scroll area ends at y = 642, so the row starts outside the visible\narea. The test is red on the current layout.",
