      "message": "fix(ui): the machine action row stands above the visible bottom at 720 px\n\nA review found the first fix (Refresh beside the Library combo) was not\nenough: the \"Load other\", \"Edit\" and \"Clear\" row still ended 20 px below\nthe top of the pane's Close footer, so the buttons were outside the page.\nMoving the Library row one row up cannot pay for 26 px.\n\nThe page now reclaims the height in three places, and keeps every label,\nword and command:\n\n- machine_page draws its rows at a 2 px vertical gap of its own (ROW_GAP)\n  instead of the shell's 3 px. The gap is set on the page's own Ui, which\n  the scroll area rebuilds each frame, so no other page changes.\n- The machine overview readout uses a 2 px row gap (OVERVIEW_GAP).\n  machine_grid takes the row gap as a parameter; the machine editor\n  header keeps its 4 px (machine_grid::ROW_GAP).\n- The two prose lines of the ownership block (setup_pages::ownership) are\n  drawn small and dimmed, like the machine page's own help line. In the\n  274 px pane each wrapped to three lines of 15 px; each now takes two\n  lines of 10 px. Their words and AccessKit labels are unchanged.\n\nMeasured in shell_harness() at 1280x720, Tormach 770MX loaded. The\nProperties leaf spans y = 104..682 and the Close footer starts at\ny = 648. The action row moved from y = 644..668 (below the footer edge)\nto y = 570..594. The pin test\nthe_machine_page_buttons_fit_without_scrolling_at_720_px is green; so\nare the machine page behaviour tests and layout_page_setup_machine.\n\ndocs/decisions/2105-machine-buttons-720.md is corrected: the page's\nbuttons are \"Load other\", \"Edit\" and \"Clear\" (the file named a button\n\"New\", which does not exist), and it states the measured result.",
